{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Two hundred she-goats and twenty he-goats.</b> He placed the she-goats first, following their custom in every flock, that the she-goats and he-goats precede the other animals; and so it is written (Jeremiah 50:8): ״והיו כעתודים לפני צאן״. And furthermore, their males are more numerous than those of the others. After that, camels, for the males were 15 and the females 15, since they and their young are 30 altogether; then remained cows and donkeys, whose males are equal, and they are ten. And he placed the pure (species) before the impure, and in all of them he placed the females first, for they are more numerous than the males." "<b>There is</b> also an interpretation that this gift is arranged according to the number of the months of gestation: for the gestation period of goats and sheep is five months, and that of camels six months, and that of cows nine months, and that of donkeys twelve months." "<b>And now:</b> according to what I wrote above, that he did not wish to open to him with 'flock' in the verse ״ויהי לי שור וחמור״ — why did he now open the gift with she-goats and he-goats, when they are of the species of flock? As in the manner written concerning the Passover of Egypt (Exodus 12:5): ״משכו וקחו לכם צאן״, and it is written: ״מן הכבשים ומן העזים תקחו״, and it is written (Leviticus 1:10): ״ואם מן הצאן קרבנו מן הכשבים או מן העזים לעולה״." "<b>And the matter is</b> that before he prayed his prayer, he did not wish that the angels should open to him in the language of 'flock,' for it would be a cause to arouse hatred and a reminder of liability to recall to him former things. But now, after he had prayed, he did not fear him at all; on the contrary, he wished to frighten him, and he opened to him with goats to say: if your intention is to fight me, you will not be able, for I received the blessings by means of two kids of goats, and he said to me (Genesis 27:29): ״הוה גביר לאחיך ולך אמר ואת אחיך תעבוד״. And because of this he mentioned to him at the end donkeys and asses' colts, that is: you are destined to fall into the hand of my sons at the end, in the days of the Messiah, of whom it is written (Zechariah 9:9): ״גילי מאד בת ציון הריעי בת ירושלים הנה מלכך יבא לך צדיק ונושע הוא עני ורוכב על חמור ועל עיר בן אתונות״. And so he frightened him by allusion in this gift, at its opening and at its closing." "<b>And it is</b> a well-known matter that according to the wealth and status of Jacob and Esau, the value of this gift would not have been so equal were it not that it contains allusions concerning the future." "<b>And our master Hananel, of blessed memory, wrote</b> that the total of the heads of cattle in this gift-offering was 450 (תק\"ן) heads; therefore the kingdom of Edom preceded the kingdom of Israel by 450 (תק\"ן) years."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:21.099080497Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}